course: dictionary
lesson: 3393
title: Big words for big journeys
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An expedition is a long, organised journey to a faraway place, usually to explore, study or climb. «Magellan's expedition made the first voyage around the world, from 1519 to 1522.» The words long, voyage and around the world tell you the trip was huge and planned, so expedition means a big journey.
explain: The same word can also mean the group of people making the journey. «The expedition set off in 1519» means the crew left, not the trip itself. To check, swap in journey or crew and see if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Clues help you pick the right meaning. Words like scientists, study, mountains or the South Pole point to a serious expedition. In everyday talk, people sometimes joke. «We had a shopping expedition on Saturday» means a short trip with a purpose, said with a smile.
fact: An expedition is a long, organised journey to a far place, often to explore, study or climb.
fact: «Expedition» can also mean the group of people making the journey.
fact: Informally, and as a joke, a short trip with a purpose can be called an expedition, such as a «shopping expedition».
fact: «Roald Amundsen first sailed the Northwest Passage between 1903 and 1906.»
fact: Useful phrases: go on an expedition, a scientific expedition, an expedition to the South Pole.
exercise: «Magellan's expedition made the first voyage around the world.» What is an expedition? | A sandwich eaten on a hill | *A long, organised journey to a far place | A list of things to buy | A short bus ride to school
exercise: In «The expedition had twenty sailors on board», what does expedition mean? | A type of ship | *The group of people making the journey | A thick winter coat | A map of the sea
exercise: Mum says, «Our shopping expedition took two hours.» What does expedition mean here? | A journey to the South Pole | *A short trip with a purpose, said as a joke | A long, dangerous climb | A scientific study of animals
test: «Scientists went on an expedition to study penguins.» Why did they go? | To win a race | To buy new shoes | To climb a tree | *To explore and study
test: «The explorers planned a scientific expedition to the mountains.» Which word shows the trip was for learning? | mountains | explorers | *scientific | planned
exam: Which sentence uses expedition to mean the group of people on the journey? | «We had a shopping expedition on Saturday.» | «The expedition was a long walk to the shops.» | *«The expedition sang songs around the fire.» | «She went on an expedition to the South Pole.»
